# One line ending in the repository; the working tree gets the platform's.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts are checked out with CRLF or the shell mis-reads them.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.vbs  text eol=crlf

# Binary, never diffed or line-ending-converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.node binary

# Generated; keep it out of diffs but in the repository.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated

# brandkit bundles, verified by a hash of every file: stored exactly as the
# kit wrote them, because `brandkit check` compares bytes and `eol=lf` above
# would rewrite any the kit happened to write with CRLF. Two of them did until
# kit 1.56.1, which now writes LF everywhere - this rule is what made a fresh
# clone verify before that, and what will hold if it ever changes again.
# Still diffed: a rebuild that changes the typeface or a corner radius shows
# up as a line in template/tokens.css, which is how it gets noticed.
app/brand/** -text
docs/brand/** -text

# Ours, not the kit's, and the only file in there that is written by hand.
app/brand/README.md text eol=lf
